    "turn_text": "toolbox with Fourth of July savings. Wow, we're already here with Fourth of July savings. This is great. Unselect top brand cordless power from the Home Depot, whether you're working on a fence, a planer box, or a new workbench. You'll get power and convenience with the Ryobi one plus 18 volt two tool kit. From the Home Depot, now at a lower price of $99 was $139. That's why you can get 4th of July savings on the cordless power you need to make summer projects easier than ever. Right now at the Home Depot. Reflecting on your time in the house, what gives you hope for the future of the party, the Congress, and how we make policy in this country and what gives you concern. I am very hopeful for the party because I just think the future with leadership like Akim is so bright, but I'm not that hopeful for United States Congress. I pray for you all all the time. I don't know how you work with certain people you work with up there. Well, you know, black people have had historically we had to fight just the right to breathe, the right to live, right? So I think we have the edge, Picard, to lead. And that's why Hakeem is going to be so effective a speaker. And that is why when you see now the young black people running and winning these seats in office, this was what gives me hope for a long time. And I think it was Joy Reed who said very recently that for so long, Barbara Lee was the squad, the only squad member. Okay. And so I've had to fight a lot of these battles by myself as a black woman progressive but reproductive freedom right to an abortion ended up hide a limit voting against authorization to use force voting against funding. you know, military, DOD funding, waste broaden abuse, $150 million waste broaden abuse. We can use to house the unsheltered and for education and for health care. So I've been out there forever. And so now what gives me hope is, you know, we got a real progressive movement within the House of Representatives with our black elected officials, our black members of Congress, our progressive members of Congress. And so it's not just Barbara Lee is the squad. There is a real powerful, effective, principled squad, a group of progressive members of Congress who get it, who understand why we have to have structural and systemic change, but who also are practical and how to negotiate with Republicans and Democrats and who are getting the job done. And so, finally, just in reflecting on",
