    "turn_idx": 52,
    "turn_text": "go to work. Yes, we need more development and diplomacy. So we're constantly fighting all those battles. And I say, if we don't do anything, then that's to do no harm. And that's a good thing because you don't want anything done that's bad. And that's what they're about is taking and rolling the clock back. So a lot of people say, oh, that's a good point. We never thought about it when we say it's to do nothing, Congress, because it is. They're not, you know, but you don't want them to do a lot because it's damage. Makes sense to me. Shifting gears to the race for the White House. When you talk to voters, and I know you're one of the more impressive surrogates we have, because you can bridge the gap between the more moderate, maybe former blue dog Democrats and the progressive movement. What issues are motivating voters this cycle? And how well do you think the Biden White House and the campaign have been responding to them? Well, you know, the economic issues are first and foremost, Bakari. Even though we have strong economic growth, job creation, unprecedented job creation. But people are still feeling the pain because of the cost of living. Housing is a big issue. Student loan debt, a big issue. Healthcare. Grosser, yeah. People can't afford to live and wage growth has not been in our communities, has not grown at the same pace as inflation and as the cost of living. And so I'm hearing that over and over and over again. Even though the Biden-Harris administration had done everything they could do in all the economic indicators and showing that inflation slowly is going down, job growth is, you know, all of the issues in terms of job creation, that inflation reduction act, chips, all of the recovery efforts. And also, you know, I have to remind people, and this is a crass way to say it, but you have to remember, COVID. And our people were dying disproportionately of COVID, thanks to Donald Trump. I mean, he would not enact policies that would save lives. And so the Biden-Harris campaign came in and immediately got the COVID pandemic under control, the economics and the health impacts of it. And so I say to people sometimes, I said,",
